that judgment escaped attention of generations thereafter due to the label “dissenting”. The majority, with respect, 
is not always right and it is for the posterity to assess the truth of the opinion of the minority. In C. A. RII 46 
2023 dated 15.02.2024 I have argued that both stare decisis and cursus curiae are matters of practice (conclusion of 
the reasoning at page 64 of that judgment). The importance of dissenting opinion in shaping up the legal landscape of 
